$
$ Database for high entropy alloys version 5.0, May 2023
$ The elements Al, Co, Cr, Fe, Mn, Ni, V and C are included.
$
$ Database created 2016.11.13 by Bengt Hallstedt.
$ Version 2 created 2017.01.17
$ Version 2b created 2017.07.24
$ Version 2c created 2019.10.15
$ Version 3 created 2020.02.10 and 2020.11.20
$ Version 4 created 2021.03.22
$ Version 4b created 2021.05.07
$ Version 4c created 2022.08.29
$ Version 5 created 2023.04.18
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$
$ This database is open access under the CC BY license. 
$ https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
$
$ For comments and questions please contact:
$
$ Dr. Bengt Hallstedt
$ Institute for Materials Applications in Mechanical Engineering (IWM)
$ RWTH Aachen University, Aachen, Germany
$ b.hallstedt@iwm.rwth-aachen.de
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$
$ 2023.08.22: G(MV3_A15,CO:CR) removed because MV3_A15 becomes stable in Co-Cr
$             below 673 K.
$
$ Version 5 contains a number of updates of systems not containg V, the most
$ important being Co-Cr-Mn. The updates were made as a preparation to
$ publishing the Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Mn-Ni-C part of the database.
$ HIGH_SIGMA has been removed from the database. HIGH_SIGMA originates from
$ the Cr-Mn binary where it has been shown to be non-existent by J.-M. Joubert
$ (Intermetallics, 146, 107580(2022)). The Cr-Mn binary is reasonably
$ reproduced when HIGH_SIGMA is simply removed. In the same paper Cr3Mn5 was
$ found to be a ternary nitride. This phase was also removed.
$ The following systems were updated: Cr-Mn, Al-Co-C, Al-Cr-C, Al-Ni-C,
$ Co-Cr-Mn, Cr-Fe-Mn, Cr-Mn-Ni and Ni-V-C.
$
$ Version 4c: Missing type definition for magnetism added to CEMENTITE_D011.
$
$ Version 4b contains a new version of Fe-Ni from G. Cacciamani et al. 2010.
$ The ternary systems Al-Fe-Ni, Co-Fe-Ni, Cr-Fe-Ni, Fe-Mn-Ni and Fe-Ni-C
$ were checked and to a minor extent modified.
$
$ Version 4 contains a preliminary inclusion of V. Many ternary systems with V
$ are still missing, in particular those with Al. A number of ternary systems
$ from the Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-V system assessed by W.-M. Choi et al. 2018 and 2019
$ have been modified (several new binaries) and included.
$
$ 2021.03.22: The revised version of Al-Co-Fe is included.
$ 2021.01.15: L(FCC_A1,AL,CO,NI:VA;2) corrected.
$
$ Version 3 is considered complete with respect to the elements
$ Al, Co, Cr, Fe, Mn, Ni and C.
$ Version 3 contains a number of new ternary systems and a few modified
$ binary systems. Co-Cr-Fe is modified from W.-M. Choi et al. 2019. Co-Cr-Mn
$ is modified in a similar fashion (though without experimental data to verify).
$ These two modifications makes sigma stable in the Cantor alloy between
$ 360°C and 600°C, which is a bit lower than experiment.
$
$ All ternary systems with Al are now included. Those previously included
$ have been revised.
$
$ Version 2c is compatible with Thermo-Calc 2019b (GES6). For this unused
$ parameters have been removed (mostly element paramaters for phases that are
$ not included in the database) and no abbreviations for phase names are used.
$
$ Version 2b contains ternary parameters for Al-Fe-Ni from L. Zhang et al. 2009
$ instead of L. Zhang and Y. Du 2007. The older assessment results in far too
$ high liquidus temperatures in the Al-poor part (including the AlFe-AlNi
$ section) of the system.
$
$ Version 2 additionally contains the elements Al and C. Important new
$ phases are (Co,Ni)Al-B2 and kappa (Co,Fe,Mn,Ni)3AlC.
$
$ Version 1 contains the elements Co, Cr, Fe, Mn and Ni (i.e. the "classical"
$ Cantor system). It contains evaluations for all ten binary and ten ternary
$ systems. However, Co-Cr-Fe, Co-Cr-Mn and Co-Mn-Ni are simply extrapolations
$ from their respective binaries. For Co-Cr-Mn and Co-Mn-Ni there is an almost
$ complete lack of experimental data. For Co-Cr-Fe there are experimental data,
$ but the system has not yet been assessed.
$
$ The following section applies only to version 1 of the database:
$ There is a 4-sublattice model for fcc and a 2-sublattice model for bcc.
$ These models are excluded by default, but can be included for calculations
$ at low temperature and/or close the binaries where they are stable.
$ L1_2 is stable as FeNi3 and MnNi3, L1_0 as MnNi-LT and B2 as CoFe and MnNi-HT.
$ At low temperature in some ternaries there are regions of ordered fcc (L1_2)
$ which are questionable. When FCC_4SL is included calculations can be rather
$ slow.
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 TEMP-LIM 298.15 6000.00 !
$
$ELEMENT NAME  REF. STATE               ATOMIC MASS H298-H0    S298    !
$
 ELEMENT VA   VACUUM                      0.0          0.0      0.0    ! 
 ELEMENT AL   FCC_A1                     26.98154   4540.      28.30   ! 
 ELEMENT C    GRAPHITE                   12.011     1054.0      5.7423 ! 
 ELEMENT CO   HCP_A3                     58.9332    4765.567   30.0400 ! 
 ELEMENT CR   BCC_A2                     51.996     4050.0     23.5429 ! 
 ELEMENT FE   BCC_A2                     55.847     4489.0     27.2797 ! 
 ELEMENT MN   CBCC_A12                   54.9380    4995.696   32.2206 ! 
 ELEMENT NI   FCC_A1                     58.69      4787.0     29.7955 ! 
 ELEMENT V    BCC_A2                     50.9415    4507.0     30.89   ! 
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Phase definitions
$
 PHASE LIQUID:L % 1 1 !
 CONST LIQUID:L : AL C CO CR FE MN NI V : !
$
$ Fcc (cF4, Fm-3m) and MeX (cF8, Fm-3m)
$
 PHASE FCC_A1 %A 2 1 1 !
 CONST FCC_A1 : AL% CO% CR FE% MN% NI% V : C VA% : !
$
$ Disordered part of FCC_4SL, identical to FCC_A1
$
 PHASE A1_FCC %A 2 1 1 !
 CONST A1_FCC : AL CO CR FE MN NI V : C VA% : !
$
$ Prototype AuCu3 (cP4, Pm-3m, L1_2) and AuCu (tP4, P4/mmm, L1_0)
$
 PHASE FCC_4SL:F %AY 5 0.25 0.25 0.25 0.25 1 !
 CONST FCC_4SL:F : AL CO CR FE MN NI V : AL CO CR FE MN NI V 
                 : AL CO CR FE MN NI V : AL CO CR FE MN NI V : C VA% :  !
$
$ Bcc (cI2, Im-3m)
$
 PHASE BCC_A2 %B 2 1 3 !
 CONST BCC_A2 : AL CO CR% FE% MN% NI V% VA : C VA% : !
$
$ Disordered part of B2_BCC, added 0.1 J/mol to A2_BCC
$
 PHASE A2_BCC %B 2 1 3 !
 CONST A2_BCC : AL CO CR FE MN NI V VA : C VA% : !
$
$ Prototype CsCl (cP2, Pm-3m)
$
 PHASE B2_BCC %BO 3 0.5 0.5 3 !
 CONST B2_BCC : AL CO CR FE MN% NI V VA : AL CO CR FE MN NI% V VA : C VA% : !
$
$ Hcp (hP2, P6_3/mmc) and Me2X (NiAs-type, hP4, P6_3/mmc, B8_1)
$
 PHASE HCP_A3 %A 2 1 0.5 !
 CONST HCP_A3 : AL CO% CR FE MN NI V : C VA% : !
$
$ Prototype C (cF8, Fd-3m)
$
 PHASE DIAMOND_A4 % 1 1 !
 CONST DIAMOND_A4 : C : !
$
$ Prototype C (hP4, P6_3/mmc)
$
 PHASE GRAPHITE_A9 % 1 1 !
 CONST GRAPHITE_A9 : C : !
$
$ Prototype alpha-Mn (cI58, I-43m)
$
 PHASE CBCC_A12 %A 2 1 1 !
 CONST CBCC_A12 : AL CO CR FE MN% NI V : C VA% : !
$
$ Prototype beta-Mn (cP20, P4_132)
$
 PHASE CUB_A13 % 2 1 1 !
 CONST CUB_A13 : AL CO CR FE MN% NI V : C VA% : !
$
$ Prototype Al4C3 (hR7, R-3m)
$
 PHASE AL4C3_D71 % 2 4 3 !
 CONST AL4C3_D71 : AL : C : !
$
$ Prototype Al9Co2 (mP22, P2_1/c), also Al9FeNi (tau-1)
$
 PHASE AL9CO2 % 2 9 2 !
 CONST AL9CO2 : AL : CO FE NI : !
$
$ Prototype o-Al13Co4 (oP102, Pmn2_1), Pnma at high T
$
 PHASE O_AL13CO4 % 2 0.76 0.24 !
 CONST O_AL13CO4 : AL : CO : !
$
$ Space group C2/m
$
 PHASE Y_AL13CO4 % 2 0.755 0.245 !
 CONST Y_AL13CO4 : AL : CO : !
$
$ Space group P2/m
$
 PHASE AL3CO % 2 0.745 0.255 !
 CONST AL3CO : AL : CO% NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al5Co2 (hP28, P6_3/mmc), also Al10Fe3Ni (tau-2), AlMnNi-tau-1
$
 PHASE AL5CO2_D811 % 2 5 2 !
 CONST AL5CO2_D811 : AL : AL CO% FE MN NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al60Mn11Ni4 (oC156, Cmcm)
$
 PHASE ALCOMN_T % 3 0.794  0.02  0.186 !
 CONST ALCOMN_T : AL : CO : MN : !
$
$ Decagonal, P10/mmm
$
 PHASE ALCONI_T1 % 3 14 1 5 !
 CONST ALCONI_T1 : AL : AL CO NI : CO NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al9Co2Ni (oI96, Immm)
$
 PHASE ALCONI_T2 % 2 3 1 !
 CONST ALCONI_T2 : AL : CO NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al18Co5Ni3 (mC26, C2/m)
$
 PHASE ALCONI_T3 % 3 9 2 2 !
 CONST ALCONI_T3 : AL : CO : CO NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al45V7 (mC104, C2/m)
$
 PHASE AL7CR % 2 7 1 !
 CONST AL7CR : AL : AL CR% FE MN NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al5Cr (mC732, C2/c)
$
 PHASE AL11CR2 % 2 11 2 !
 CONST AL11CR2 : AL% FE : AL CR% FE MN : !
$
$ Prototype MoSi2 (tI6, I4/mmm)
$
 PHASE ALCR2_C11B % 2 1 2 !
 CONST ALCR2_C11B : AL% CR MN : AL CR% MN : !
$
$ Pearson oI366, Immm
$
 PHASE ALCRFE_O % 2 0.72 0.28 !
 CONST ALCRFE_O : AL : AL CR FE : !
$
$ Prototype Al70Mn17Pd13, decagonal
$
 PHASE ALCRFE_D3 % 2 0.72 0.28 !
 CONST ALCRFE_D3 : AL : AL CR FE : !
$
$ Pearson hR1389, R-3
$
 PHASE ALCRFE_H % 3 1 0.09 0.22 !
 CONST ALCRFE_H : AL : CR : AL CR FE : !
$
$ Pearson oC584, Cmcm
$
 PHASE ALCRFE_E % 3 0.77 0.21 0.02 !
 CONST ALCRFE_E : AL : CR : FE : !
$
$ Prototype Al8Cr2Ni (hP228, P6_3), tau-1
$
 PHASE AL8CR2NI % 3 8 2 1 !
 CONST AL8CR2NI : AL% CR NI : AL CR% NI : AL CR NI% : !
$
$ (mP*, P2_1 or P2_1/m)
$
 PHASE ALCRNI_T2 % 3 0.8 0.11 0.09 !
 CONST ALCRNI_T2 : AL : CR : NI : !
$
$ (hR*, R3 or R-3)
$
 PHASE ALCRNI_T3 % 3 0.82 0.15 0.03 !
 CONST ALCRNI_T3 : AL : CR : NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al5Fe2 (oC24, Cmcm)
$ Al5Fe2 does not have the Al5Co2 (D8_11) structure
$
 PHASE AL5FE2 % 2 5 2 !
 CONST AL5FE2 : AL : CO CR FE% MN NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al2Fe (aP18, P1)
$
 PHASE AL2FE % 2 2 1 !
 CONST AL2FE : AL : CO CR FE% MN NI : !
$
$ SG P6_3/mmc
$
 PHASE ALFEMN_PHI % 3 0.7 0.15 0.15 !
 CONST ALFEMN_PHI : AL : AL MN : FE MN : !
$
$ SG P10/mmc, decagonal
$
 PHASE ALFEMN_D3 % 3 0.7 0.08 0.22 !
 CONST ALFEMN_D3 : AL : AL FE : FE MN : !
$
$ Prototype AlFeMn-zeta (hP227, P6_3/m), also AlMnNi-T2 (kappa)
$
 PHASE ALFEMN_ZETA % 2 4 1 !
 CONST ALFEMN_ZETA : AL : FE MN NI : !
$
$ Decagonal (quasicrystal) tau-3
$
 PHASE AL71FE5NI24 % 3 0.71 0.05 0.24 !
 CONST AL71FE5NI24 : AL : FE : NI : !
$
$ Prototype mu-Al4Mn (hP574, P6_3/mmc)
$ also suggested: Al4Cr (oC584, Cmcm, epsilon-Al4Cr)
$
 PHASE AL4M_MU % 2 4 1 !
 CONST AL4M_MU : AL : AL CR% FE MN% NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al13Fe4 (mC102, C2/m)
$
 PHASE M_AL13M4 % 3 0.6275 0.235 0.1375 !
 CONST M_AL13M4 : AL : CO% CR FE% MN NI : AL VA : !
$
$ Prototype Al12W (cI26, Im-3)
$
 PHASE AL12MN % 2 12 1 !
 CONST AL12MN : AL : CR FE MN% : !
$
$ Prototype Al6Mn (oC28, Cmcm)
$
 PHASE AL6MN_D2H % 2 6 1 !
 CONST AL6MN_D2H : AL : CR FE MN% : !
$
$ Prototype lambda-Al4Mn (hP586, P6_3/m)
$
 PHASE AL4MN_LAMBDA % 2 0.81162 0.18838 !
 CONST AL4MN_LAMBDA : AL : MN : !
$
$ Prototype Al11Mn4 (aP15, P-1)
$
 PHASE AL11MN4_LT % 2 11 4 !
 CONST AL11MN4_LT : AL : CR MN% NI : !
$
$ Prototype Al3Mn (oP156, Pnma)
$
 PHASE AL11MN4_HT % 2 29 10 !
 CONST AL11MN4_HT : AL% CR MN : CR FE MN% NI : !
$
