$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Co-V
$
$ P. Wang, T. Hammerschmidt, U.R. Kattner, G.B. Olson,
$ Calphad, 68, 101729(2020).
$
$ Checked against paper and author's tdb. Checked at 6000 K.
$
$ Modified to be compatible with mpea-04.
$ The sigma model was changed to a "standard" (not add-on) 10:4:16 model
$ without magnetic contribution. The sigma parameters were refitted to
$ reproduce invariant equilibria to within 3 K. The sigma phase field is
$ somewhat wider towards Co at intermediate temperatures (600 to 1200 K).
$ In 20Wan there is a flip in sublattice occupation from Co on the 3rd
$ sublattice to the 2nd sublattice. This produces a miscibility gap at low
$ temperature around x(V)=0.3. The magnetic transition might contribute
$ to this.
$
$ G(CO3V,V:V) was changed to the value used in Ni-V.
$ This changes the fcc = Co3V + sigma equilibrium from 1285 K to 1282 K and
$ the composition of Co3V from x(V)=0.311 to x(V)=0.309.
$
$ V was added on the first sublattice of CoV3. The changes the
$ sigma + bcc = CoV3 equilibrium from 1297 to 1308 K.
$
$ The B2 ordering energy was calculated from the difference between L1_0 and B2
$ from ab initio calculations by 20Wan in their supplemental material.
$ (E(B2) - E(L1_0) = 6.68 kJ/mol-atoms). Since already Delta-H for bcc-A2
$ is about the same as for L1_0, the B2 ordering enrgy is set to zero.
$
$ Sigma is modelled with an add-on model. In the paper the model is fractional
$ which is converted to integer in this dataset.
$
$ There is no hcp interaction included in the paper. Using the same interaction
$ as for fcc makes hcp stable above Co3V. The hcp interaction was set to
$ 10 kJ/mol less than the fcc interaction.
$
$ The parameters for CoV3 are misprinted in the paper.
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,CO,V;0),,                -60297.6+2.6502*T;,,          N 20Wan !
 PAR  L(LIQUID,CO,V;1),,                -10417.3;,,                   N 20Wan !
 PAR  L(LIQUID,CO,V;2),,                +18698.7;,,                   N 20Wan !
$
 PAR  L(FCC_A1,CO,V:VA;0),,             -69595.2+11.2314*T;,,         N 20Wan !
 PAR  L(FCC_A1,CO,V:VA;1),,             -41802.8+4.2329*T;,,          N 20Wan !
