$ Cr-Mn
$
$ From B.-J. Lee 1993 (Included in LB Vol. 2)
$
$ B.-J. Lee, Metall. Trans. A, 24, 1919-33(1993).
$
$ Checked against LB and paper. Checked at 6000 K.
$
$ Using in-situ neutron diffraction J.-M. Joubert (Intermetallics, 146,
$ 107580(2022)) showed that high-sigma does not exist. Above the sigma phase
$ field there is a bcc phase field. A very reasonable phase diagram can be
$ achieved by simply removing the high-sigma phase.
$
$ The CBCC_A12 interaction referred to as 98Lee is an old parameter from 1991.
$ It is used by mistake in COST and LB.
$
