$ Fe-V
$
$ From W. Huang 1991 (Included in LB Vol. 3)
$
$ W. Huang, Z. Metallkd., 82, 391-401(1991).
$
$ Checked against LB and paper. Checked at 6000K.
$
$ Endmember value for G(SIGMA_D8B,V:V:V) changed from 02Sun to 06Slu.
$ This causes a decrease of the sigma max T from 1515 K to 1500 K.
$ This could be compensated by a slight increase in sigma stability,
$ but has not been done yet.
$ This is not included in the 91Hua binary dataset.
$
$ W. Huang used the 8:4:18 model for the sigma phase (SIGMA_OLD). This was
$ changed to 10:4:16 (SIGMA_D8B) for LB. The change of model shifts
$ the maximum to higher V content. Max at x(V)=0.485 for SIGMA_OLD
$ and x(V)=0.517 for SIGMA_D8B.
$
