$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Mn-Ni
$
$ A. Walnsch, M.J. Kriegel, M. Rudolph, M. Motylenko, O. Fabrichnaya,
$ A. Leineweber, Calphad, 64, 78-89(2019).
$
$ Checked against paper and author's tdb. Checked at 6000 K.
$
$ Changed 2sl fcc (FCC_L12 and L10_SOLO) to 4sl using option F.
$ Invariant equilibria involving L1_0 and B2 are 2 to 3 K higher with the
$ 2sl version.
$
$ Modified from 10Liu. Interactions for CBCC_A12 and CUB_A13 are changed. This
$ is not discussed in the paper, but shown in their phase diagram. Maybe the
$ change was forgotten by the authors. The cbcc-A12 and cub-A13 Gibbs energy
$ curves are now much closer to the fcc curve, which considerably improves
$ the fit of the cub-A13 region in (at least) the Al-Mn-Ni system.
$
$ The existence of the MnNi2 compound has been questioned.
$
$ There seems to be a magnetic miscibility gap (with Nishizawa horn) in the
$ fcc phase on the Ni-rich side below about 500 K. For some reason it
$ continues as a very thin miscibility gap up to the solidus.
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,MN,NI;0),,               -44423.1238-2.35314123*T;,,   N 10Liu !
 PAR  L(LIQUID,MN,NI;1),,               +11941.36-6.85220387*T;,,     N 10Liu !
