$ Ni-V
$
$ M. Noori, B. Hallstedt, Calphad, 65, 273-81(2019).
$
$ Checked against paper. Checked at 6000 K.
$
$ This dataset contains a 3-SL 10:4:16 model for sigma and solubility ranges
$ for Ni3V and NiV3, but not for Ni8V and Ni2V.
$
$ The fcc ordering parameter was set to zero. This is possibly questionable.
$ The energy difference between the stable Ni3V (D0_22) and L1_2 is about
$ 8 kJ/mol-atoms according to ab initio calculations (19Noo). Already the
$ difference between D0_22 and disordered fcc is less than this. I.e. there
$ is no room for an additional ordering energy, although there should
$ logically be one (at least according to a simple BW-model).
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,NI,V;0),,                -67757+5.77*T;,,              N 19Noo !
