$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Ternary systems
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Al-Co-C
$
$ W. Zheng, S. He, J. Wang, H. Mao, J. Phase Equiib. Diffus., 39, 538-48(2018).
$
$ Checked against paper.
$
$ Al-Co from 17Wan is replaced by 19Noo, but as 19Noo is modified from
$ 19Ost/17Wan/13Ste changes should be minimal.
$
$ The ternary bcc interaction is reduced to decrease the C solubility in B2.
$ Probably the interaction can be set to zero, but an interaction is kept
$ nevertheless.
$
$ Al:Al kappa parameters are changed to those used in mpea-4c.
$
$ Differences are small, except C solubility in B2, which is (intentionally)
$ clearly lower.
$
$ The L --> fcc + B2 + kappa reaction is at 1625 K instead of 1611 K. Same
$ as in the non-mod dataset.
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,C,CO;0),,             +ZERO;,,                      N 18Zhe3 !
 PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,C,CO;1),,             -162000;,,                    N 18Zhe3 !
