$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Al-Co-Ni
$
$ Y. Wang, G. Cacciamani, Calphad, 61, 198-210(2018).
$
$ Checked against paper.
$
$ Al-Co is from 20Noo instead of 16Liu.
$ Fcc changed from 2SL to 4SL.
$ Modification of M_AL13CO4
$
$ Parameters for M_AL13CO4 (= AL13FE4, M_AL13M4) in Al-Ni are taken from 09Zha2
$ (Al-Fe-Ni). The Ni solubility in Al13Co4 seems a bit high towards high
$ temperature. At lower temperatures, where T2 is present, the match is good.
$
$ A rather large number of adjustments were made to approximately reproduce
$ the phase diagrams published in 18Wang. In particular the B2_BCC phase
$ was (and still is) problematic. The liquidus/solidus of the Al-poor side
$ of B2 is not well reproduced. The B2 + fcc eutectic is much lower than
$ in 18Wan and seem to be in conflict with old data from Schramm 1941. There
$ seem to be no direct data on liquidus/solidus for the Al-poor part of
$ the system. On the other hand, the behaviour of the B2 phase at high
$ temperature in 18Wan also does not seem to be reasonable.
$
$ This system (at least B2, fcc, L1_2 and liquid) would need to be reoptimized,
$ but the lack of liquidus/solidus data makes this severely problematic.
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,CO,NI;0),,            -225383+12.244*T;,,           N 16Wan1 !
 PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,CO,NI;1),,            +11080+27.616*T;,,            N 18Wan !
$ Parameter from paper below
$PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,CO,NI;2),,            +40143+23.207*T;,,            N 18Wan !
$ Parameter from author's tdb below
 PAR  L(LIQUID,AL,CO,NI;2),,            +59143+26.207*T;,,            N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  L(FCC_A1,AL,CO,NI:VA;0),,         +20560-9.113*T;,,             N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(FCC_A1,AL,CO,NI:VA;1),,         -25000;,,                     N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(FCC_A1,AL,CO,NI:VA;2),,         -22000;,,                     N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  L(A1_FCC,AL,CO,NI:VA;0),,         +20560-9.113*T;,,             N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(A1_FCC,AL,CO,NI:VA;1),,         -25000;,,                     N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(A1_FCC,AL,CO,NI:VA;2),,         -22000;,,                     N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  G(FCC_4SL,AL:AL:CO:NI:VA),,       +FAL2CONI;,,                  N 18Wan !
 PAR  G(FCC_4SL,CO:CO:AL:NI:VA),,       +FALCO2NI;,,                  N 18Wan !
 PAR  G(FCC_4SL,NI:NI:AL:CO:VA),,       +FALCONI2;,,                  N 20Hal4 !
$
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,AL,CO:NI:VA;0),,         -15000;,,                     N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,NI:AL,CO:VA;0),,         -15000;,,                     N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,AL,CO:NI:VA;1),,         -15000;,,                     N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,NI:AL,CO:VA;1),,         -15000;,,                     N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,CO,NI:AL:VA;0),,         -7500;,,                      N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(B2_BCC,AL:CO,NI:VA;0),,         -7500;,,                      N 20Hal4 !
$
 PAR  L(AL9CO2,AL:CO,NI;0),,            -34000+15.5*T;,,              N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(AL9CO2,AL:CO,NI;1),,            -95414+70*T;,,                N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  L(M_AL13M4,AL:CO,NI:AL;0),,       -6000+2.95*T;,,               N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(M_AL13M4,AL:CO,NI:VA;0),,       -6000+2.95*T;,,               N 20Hal4 !
$
 PAR  L(AL3CO,AL:CO,NI;0),,             -6500;,,                      N 20Hal4 !
$
 PAR  L(AL5CO2_D811,AL:CO,NI;0),,       -70002+32*T;,,                N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(AL5CO2_D811,AL:CO,NI;1),,       -30325+25*T;,,                N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  L(AL3NI_D011,AL:CO,NI;0),,        -29200+7*T;,,                 N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  G(AL3NI2_D513,AL:CO:NI),,         +3*GBCCAL+2*GBCCCO+GBCCNI
             -250000;,,                                               N 18Wan !
 PAR  G(AL3NI2_D513,AL:NI:CO),,         +3*GBCCAL+2*GBCCNI+GBCCCO;,,  N 18Wan !
 PAR  L(AL3NI2_D513,AL:CO,NI:VA;0),,    -158428+86*T;,,               N 18Wan !
$
 PAR  L(AL4NI3,AL:CO,NI;0),,            -130000+50*T;,,               N 20Hal4 !
 PAR  L(AL4NI3,AL:CO,NI;1),,            -40000;,,                     N 20Hal4 !
$
